@* The turn-taking / barge-in trace, rendered as an event log. Open by default
   so the loop is visible as it runs; collapse it to get it out of the way.
   After the first render the <details> open state belongs to the browser:
   Blazor only patches attributes whose rendered value changed, and `open` never
   does, so re-renders don't undo a collapse.

   Newest-first without JS: the list is laid out `column-reverse` inside a plain
   scroll container, so the newest row sits at the top and a viewer at the top
   stays there as rows arrive. The DOM order stays oldest-to-newest, so assistive
   tech reads the rows in the order they happened.

   Deliberately *not* aria-live — these rows arrive several per turn and would
   flood a screen reader. The status row and transcript already carry the
   announcements a user needs (Best practice #9). *@

<section class="panel" aria-label="Diagnostics">
    <details class="diagnostics" open>
        <summary class="panel-title diag-summary">
            Diagnostics <span class="diag-count">@Events.Count</span>
        </summary>

        <div class="diag-actions">
            <button type="button" class="btn btn-small" @onclick="OnClear" disabled="@(Events.Count == 0)">
                Clear
            </button>
        </div>

        @if (Events.Count == 0)
        {
            <p class="diag-empty">
                Start a session and speak — turn events, barge-in cut-offs, and TTS
                acks show up here.
            </p>
        }
        else
        {
            <div class="diag-scroll">
                <ol class="diag-list">
                    @foreach (var evt in Events)
                    {
                        <li @key="evt.Seq" class="diag-row">
                            <span class="diag-time">@evt.FormattedAt</span>
                            <span class="diag-badge" data-channel="@evt.Channel">@evt.Channel</span>
                            <span class="diag-label">@evt.Label</span>
                            @if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(evt.Detail))
                            {
                                <span class="diag-detail">@evt.Detail</span>
                            }
                        </li>
                    }
                </ol>
            </div>
        }
    </details>
</section>

@code {
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public IReadOnlyList<DiagnosticEvent> Events { get; set; } = [];
    [Parameter] public EventCallback OnClear { get; set; }
}
